# Build artefacts.
#
# The snapshot is rebuilt with `python -m harness --build`; committing it would
# put a moving EDGAR extract in version control, and the dataset's expectations
# are resolved from whichever snapshot is in use, so a committed copy would go
# stale against the code that reads it.
#
# The cross-framework and population archives are the same kind of thing and are
# ignored for the same reason: each is an EDGAR extract for a set of issuers,
# rebuilt by `build_crossframework_snapshot.py` and `ingest_universe.py`, and the
# reports record the numbers each produced. Committing one live archive while
# ignoring its siblings would leave the repository with a different rule for the
# same artefact depending on which phase produced it.
snapshot.sqlite
snapshot.sqlite-*
snapshot-crossframework.sqlite
snapshot-crossframework.sqlite-*

# The population archive is larger than its siblings -- a stratified run over
# live EDGAR -- and what is committed from it is the *result*, universe-211.json,
# which holds the cost measurements and every classified outcome. The numbers are
# the finding; the database is reproducible with one command.
snapshot-universe.sqlite
snapshot-universe.sqlite-*

# Bulk-path inputs and output. The companyfacts documents are a moving EDGAR
# extract; the bulk archive is a build artefact of them. The *reconciliation* is
# committed -- bulk-reconcile-212.json -- because the numbers in it are the
# finding.
bulkfacts/
snapshot-bulk.sqlite
snapshot-bulk.sqlite-*

# The mixed-source merge archive and the trimmed payload it is built from. Same
# reasoning as the other archives, and the trimmed payload is *derived* from the
# fetched documents rather than fetched itself. The committed artefact is
# merge-213.json, which holds the fingerprints and the verdict.
snapshot-merge.sqlite
snapshot-merge.sqlite-*

# The full-Core-scope bulk archive, built by `fullscope_bulk.py` from the
# inventory documents with no network at all. Same reasoning as its siblings:
# the archive is a build artefact and the committed artefact is the result,
# fullscope-214.json.
snapshot-fullscope.sqlite
snapshot-fullscope.sqlite-*
collection-fullscope/

# The full-Core-scope population archive, built by `fullscope_bulk.py` from the
# bulk-facts payload with no network at all. Same reasoning as its siblings:
# the archive is a build artefact and the committed artefact is the result,
# population-215.json.
snapshot-population.sqlite
snapshot-population.sqlite-*
collection-population/

# The gate tool's own JSON, run over both archives. `score_collection_gates.py`
# prints as well as writing, and the committed artefact already carries the
# gate results, so these two are the intermediate rather than the finding.
gates-fullscope.json
gates-reference.json
gates-population.json
gates-universe.json
gates-universe-216.json
chains-universe-216.json

# Collection chains derived from the 75-issuer archive by
# `derive_collection_chains.py`. Regenerable in one command from the archive, and
# the archive itself is gitignored -- so committing these would be committing a
# measurement with no subject.
collection-universe/

# The bank payload, fetched by `fetch_source_inventory.py` for the eight SIC 60
# filers the 2.16.1 split reclassified. A moving EDGAR extract like its siblings.
bulkfacts-banks/
bulkfacts-banks-2/
submissions-banks/
fetch-banks.json
fetch-banks-2.json
fetch-banks-both.json

# The full-Core-scope bank archive. Same reasoning as its siblings: one command
# rebuilds it from `bulkfacts-banks/`.
snapshot-banks.sqlite
snapshot-banks.sqlite-*
collection-banks/
gates-banks.json
banks-217.json

# The two-stream bank archive: `companyfacts` plus `submissions`.
snapshot-banks2.sqlite
snapshot-banks2.sqlite-*
collection-banks2/
gates-banks2.json
banks2-218.json
banks2-220.json

# The corrected API-path reference for the same eight banks. Built under the
# availability contract 2.14 fixed, which is what makes the bulk/API equivalence
# chain closable at all.
snapshot-banks-api.sqlite
snapshot-banks-api.sqlite-*
collection-banks-api/
gates-banks-api.json
banks-api-220.json

# The MINING and INSURANCE population: four filers of each, none of which
# existed in any archive here before 2.23. A moving EDGAR extract and its build
# artefacts, on the same terms as their siblings.
bulkfacts-ins-min/
submissions-ins-min/
fetch-ins-min.json
candidate-sic-scan.json
snapshot-ins-min.sqlite
snapshot-ins-min.sqlite-*
collection-ins-min/
gates-ins-min.json
insmin-223.json

# The SIC 61-62 population, whose candidate names were already in the 75-issuer
# archive's own classification table. IPB has no `companyfacts` document at all --
# EDGAR returns 404 -- so seven of the eight fetched.
bulkfacts-fs/
submissions-fs/
fetch-fs.json
fetch-fs-AIXC.json
fetch-fs-FMCCH.json
fetch-fs-IPB.json
fetch-fs-OMCC.json
fetch-fs-ORXCF.json
fetch-fs-PRAA.json
fetch-fs-SLNHP.json
fetch-fs-SUIG.json
snapshot-fs.sqlite
snapshot-fs.sqlite-*
collection-fs/
gates-fs.json
fin-225.json

# 2.27 corpus. Two cohorts, measured apart: `227a-orig` is the ORIGINAL
# companyfacts for the 18 existing filers plus their newly fetched submissions,
# which is what isolates context enrichment from new filings. `227a` is the
# re-fetch that the fetch tool performs alongside submissions.
bulkfacts-227a/
bulkfacts-227a-orig/
submissions-227a/
bulkfacts-227b/
submissions-227b/
fetch-227a.json
fetch-227b.json
tickers-227b.json
snapshot-227-a1.sqlite
snapshot-227-a1.sqlite-*
collection-227-a1/
gates-227-a1.json
snapshot-227-b.sqlite
snapshot-227-b.sqlite-*
collection-227-b/
gates-227-b.json

# Source inventories, fetched by `fetch_source_inventory.py`. A moving EDGAR
# extract like the archives above: the *derived* numbers are committed (in the
# collection chains, the reports and the ledger output) and the responses are
# reproducible with one command per issuer.
inventory/
inventory/*

# Run outputs. A run of the *sealed* dataset against a real model is the
# evidence this experiment exists to produce, so those are committed; the
# verification runs of scripted targets are noise and are not.
#
#   committed:  runs/ollama-local-*/
#   ignored:    runs/scripted-*/, runs/reference-*/, runs/unknown-*/
runs/scripted-*/
runs/reference-*/
runs/unknown-*/

__pycache__/
